WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.200
"How Much Vitamin B12 Do We Need Each Day?"

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.960
There are a couple ways
to derive

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.120
vitamin B12 recommendations.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.200
One is called
the factorial approach,

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.360
in which the average
requirement of vitamin B12

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.480
is calculated as a replacement
of daily losses,

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.280
adjusted
for dietary bioavailability.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.440
So, for example,
if people lose

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.080
an average of 1 microgram
of B12 a day,

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.040
and the bioavailability
of tiny amounts of B12 from food

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.960
is assumed to be about 50%,
if you got 2 micrograms a day,

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.840
you’d absorb 1 microgram, 50%,

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.000
and that would replace
the 1 microgram

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.360
you lose every day.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.600
But that’s just
the average daily requirement,

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.080
based on average daily losses.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.720
The average requirement
would mean 50% of people

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:49.600
actually need less
and 50% need more.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.800
You don’t want
to cover the needs

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.720
of only half the population,
though,

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.000
so you add two relative
standard deviations

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.400
to cover more like 98%
of the population,

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.560
which just means
you up the average requirement

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.240
by 20 or 40%.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.280
So, if we add 20%
to that 2 micrograms a day

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.560
we came up with,

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.960
that comes out to 2.4,
which is, indeed,

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.240
exactly the RDA for B12
in the United States,

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.760
and other countries
are similar,

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.440
recommending 1.5 to 4 micrograms
a day.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:19.920
Another way to derive
B12 recommendations

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.880
is to see what dose maximizes
B12 function within the body.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:28.240
B12 is used to metabolize MMA
and homocysteine.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.000
It looks like
there’s additional benefit

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.480
up to an intake
of 6 micrograms.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.960
So instead of an RDA of 2.4,

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.040
maybe we should tell people
to get six,

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.480
since that appears to normalize

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.960
all the vitamin B12 related
variables.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.160
A subsequent, larger study
using the same principle

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.240
found the same kinds of curves,

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:49.200
maximizing B12 functionality
in the same range,

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.160
suggesting again,
instead of 2.4,

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:53.280
maybe we should tell people

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.920
to get somewhere
between 4 and 7.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.640
Since the bioavailability
of tiny amounts in the diet

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.400
is assumed to be
around 50 percent,

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.600
that would mean
we should shoot

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:05.200
for absorbing
2 to 3.5 micrograms

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.600
into our body every day.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.000
The bioavailability
of larger amounts

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.080
found in supplements
is different, though,

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.640
based on the famous
Heinrich equation.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:18.720
Down at 1 or 2 micrograms,
B12 absorption is about 50%,

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.960
but as you can see,
only about 1%

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.920
of a 2,000-microgram dose
is absorbed.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.280
Okay, so if we want
to absorb 2 to 3.5 a day

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.120
through fortified foods
or supplements,

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.160
what do we do?

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.800
Well, if we ate B12-fortified
foods at every meal,

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:33.920
three times a day,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.960
how much would we have to get
at each meal?

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:40.160
If each meal had 2 micrograms,

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.320
then we would absorb
throughout the day

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.360
0.9 times 3, or 2.7,

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.600
which would be
in the 2 to 3.5 range

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.200
we’re shooting for.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.440
So, if you had even like
three quarters of a cup (180 ml)

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:52.480
of soymilk at breakfast

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.880
and then sprinkled on
as little as one teaspoon

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.480
of certain brands
of nutritional yeast

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.360
on your lunch and dinner,
you’d be all set.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.440
Instead, if you were going
to take supplements,

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.600
how much would you
have to take each week

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.040
to absorb 2 to 3.5 micrograms’
worth a day?

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.840
Well, if you took 2,000
once a week,

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.840
that would get you 19.5,

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:15.760
which would average out
to about 2.8 a day.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.440
If you’d rather take
a supplement once a day

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.320
instead of once a week,
50 microgram tablets

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.640
are most frequently advised
and used.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.560
In theory, 50 micrograms
would get you 1.9,

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.160
and, in practice,
it looks like 50

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.560
does get you that 2 micrograms.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.160
And, indeed, in a comparison

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.720
of chewable 50-microgram
daily doses

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:37.520
to 2,000 once-a-week doses
in vegans and vegetarians

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:39.200
with marginal deficiency,

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:42.320
they both worked just as well
in bringing down MMA

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.400
and homocysteine levels.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.920
One option for fortified foods

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:49.360
that have enough for once-a-day
dosing is LeafSide,

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.840
just-add-water whole food,
plant-based meals

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.280
that have 75 micrograms
of B12 per serving.

